
<exercise workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
Find the average rate of change of <m>f(x)=2x^3</m> from <m>x=1</m> to <m>x=3</m>.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
First, compute <m>f(1)=2</m> and <m>f(3)=54</m>. Then, the average rate of change is
<me>
\frac{f(3)-f(1)}{3-1}  = \frac{54-2}{2}  = 26.
</me>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
Find the average rate of change of <m>g(t)=3t^2+4</m> between <m>t=-2</m> and <m>t=1</m>.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
First, compute <m>g(-2) = 3(-2)^2 + 4 = 16</m> and <m>g(1) = 3(1)^2+4=7</m>. Then, the average rate of change is
<me>
\frac{g(1)-g(-2)}{1-(-2)}  = \frac{7-16}{1+2}  = \frac{-9}{3} = -3.
</me>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
The table below gives the net sales of The Gap, Inc., which operates nearly <m>3000</m> clothing stores.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\hline
Year & 2005 & 2006 & 2007 & 2008 & 2009 & 2010 \\\hline
Sales (millions of dollars) & 16019 & 15923 & 15763 & 14526 & 14197 & 14660 \\\hline
\end{tabular} 
\end{center}
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
Find the average rate of change in net sales between <m>2005</m> and <m>2008</m>. Give units and interpret your answer.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The average rate of change from 2005 to 2008 is
<me>
\frac{14526 - 16019}{2008 - 2005}  = \frac{-1493}{3} = -497.7 \text{ millions of \$} / \text{year} .
</me> This means that on average, The Gap's net sales decreased by approximately <m>497.7</m> million dollars per year from 2005 to 2008.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
From 2005 to 2010, were there any one-year intervals during which the average rate of change was positive? If so, when?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Yes. From 2009 to 2010 is the only two consecutive years for which the sales increased. Therefore, this is the only one-year interval for which the ARC was positive.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>
 

<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
The graph of a function <m>f(t)</m> is given below.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\begin{axis}[grid=both,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style = very thick,
xmin=-2,xmax=5,
ymin=-3,ymax=5,
xtick={-1,1,2,3,4},
ytick={-2,-1,1,2,3,4},
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(t\), ylabel=\(f(t)\),
trig format = rad,
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=-1:4 ,thick] {-3*sin(2*3.14159/4*x) + 1};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
What is the average rate of change from <m>t=0</m> to <m>t=3</m>?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The average rate of change from <m>t=0</m> to <m>t=3</m> is
<me>
\frac{f(3)-f(0)}{3-0}  = \frac{4-1}{3}  = 1.
</me>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
What is the average rate of change from <m>t=-1</m> to <m>t=1</m>?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The average rate of change from <m>t=-1</m> to <m>t=1</m> is
<me>
\frac{f(1)-f(-1)}{1-(-1)} = \frac{-2-4}{1+1} = -3.
</me>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
What is the average rate of change from <m>t=1</m> to <m>t=4</m>?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The average rate of change from <m>t=1</m> to <m>t=4</m> is
<me>
\frac{f(4)-f(1)}{4-1}  = \frac{1-(-2)}{3}  = 1.
</me>
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>
 
